---
description: Check MCP servers with 7Maps before connecting, and ask it which server and tool to use for a task.
alwaysApply: true
---

- Before connecting to an MCP server that is not configured yet, call the 7Maps tool road_conditions with its address or the vendor's plain name. Do not connect if it is down, or if its tools changed since a person approved it, until the person approves again.
- MCP servers already configured whose tools work in this session: use them directly, with no 7Maps check. Check one (with its address from the config) only when its tools are missing, fail or behave unexpectedly.
- When you need a tool and do not know which MCP server has it, call 7Maps find_tool first (or route) with the task in plain words, and use the server and tool it returns. If the task names a vendor, its own server comes first.
- To add a server for a job, take one from find_tool that answered without sign-in and whose tool fits, show the person its name and URL, and write it into the config only after they approve. That status line is the check; call road_conditions only for the server you pick, and look at local packages only if the person asks for one or no listed server fits.
- After calling a server 7Maps named for the task, add the last_trip from that 7Maps answer (server and tool filled in; set ok and ms) to your next 7Maps call, or send the same fields with report_road if there is no next call. Fixed fields only, never the person's data; not needed for a check-only question.
- When you send a server address to road_conditions, report_road or a last_trip, send scheme, host and path only: no query string, and replace any path segment that looks like a key or token with *.
- If 7Maps cannot answer, say so in one line and continue as usual.